nue is about C$3.735B. The best recent quarter, Q1 2026 at C$980M, annualizes to about C$3.9B. Hitting C$4.2B needs roughly C$1.05B a quarter, which is 7–12% above those levels.\n- **Industry:** Transformer shipments fell 4% year on year in Q2 2026, the first decline in three years.\n- **Share:** Voltaris's share of Caldrian transformer shipments fell from 31% to 27%. Its own shipments fell 9%, the steepest drop among large makers.\n\n**Why guidance could still be met**\n- **Orders and backlog:** H1 2026 orders rose 11%. Backlog is C$5.1B, about 1.2x the guidance, and cancellations are below 1%.\n- **Fire recovery:** The Halbrook fire cut Q2 revenue. The plant restarted in August, and management expects to recover the lost shipments by mid-2027. That would add to 2027 revenue.\n\n**Why I lean toward a miss**\n- The 1.2x backlog cover is thin. The disclosure doesn't say how much of the backlog is delivered in 2027, so it is not proof of revenue.\n- The recovery is a management expectation, not something already delivered.\n- Part of the share loss is probably the outage, but the research didn't separate that from real competitive loss. If the share loss reverses, the odds improve.\n\n**Other limits**\n- No 2027 industry or share forecasts were available, and I found no data on pricing.\n- The two sub-analyses were not reconciled beyond the points above.\n\nDetails are in n2.r1 (company disclosures, leaning toward meeting guidance with little margin) and n3.r1 (industry data, central estimate C$3.5–3.8B).","ttft_ms":2793,"type":"result","duration_ms":32433,"uuid":"848ef4c7-6a78-43dd-8061-0c78392b4a42","ttft_stream_ms":2085,"time_to_request_ms":59,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":3,"resume_other":1,"process_user_input":2,"input_attachments":6,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":2,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":5,"init_frame_send":4,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":5,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":